 \noindent\textbf{Formal Foundations:}\label{sec:formal-models-secure-speculation}
 Formal definitions of speculative leakage include information-flow properties of speculative executions~\cite{cheang2019formal} and the contracts of \S\ref{sec:bg-contracts}, which Reineke surveys~\cite{reineke2026foundations}; software analyses and secure compilers build on these definitions~\cite{cauligi2022sok,cauligi2020constanttime,vassena2021blade,mosier2024serberus}. Pomset~\cite{disselkoen2019code}, axiomatic~\cite{ponce2022cats}, and out-of-order operational~\cite{guanciale2020inspectre} semantics model speculative execution, and STT comes with a pen-and-paper proof over a formal processor model~\cite{yu2019sttformal}. Formal verification~\cite{blackbox} checks secure speculation in RTL~\cite{fadiheh2019upec,fadiheh2023exhaustive,contractshadow} or in abstracted processor models~\cite{cabodi2019speculationmc}, synthesizes hardware-software contracts~\cite{mohr2024synthesizing,wang2025synthesis} and SynthLC's leakage contracts~\cite{rtl2upath} from RTL, and verifies hardware adherence to constant-time contracts~\cite{leave,dinesh2024conjunct,dinesh2025hhoudini}. Like these approaches, \toolname{} formally specifies which executions a defense forbids (\S\ref{sec:leakage-predicate}). Unlike them, it uses the specification to test the simulated defense (\S\ref{sec:synthesizer}).
 
 \noindent\textbf{Litmus Test Synthesis:}\label{sec:litmus-testing-test-generation}
-Beyond the generators of \S\ref{sec:bg-axiomatic}, litmus tests have been derived from cycles of relaxed orderings~\cite{alglave2010fences}, generated to contrast memory models~\cite{maradhaim2011litmus}, run on hardware~\cite{alglave2011litmus,perple}, and mutated to evaluate test suites~\cite{mcmutants}. The Check tools verify memory consistency model implementations, from pipelines to RTL, by analyzing axiomatic models of microarchitectures, for a suite of litmus tests or, with PipeProof, for all programs~\cite{lustig2014pipecheck,manerkar2015ccicheck,lustig2016coatcheck,trippel2017tricheck,manerkar2017rtlcheck,manerkar2018pipeproof,manerkar2020realitycheck}; memory models~\cite{memsynth} and microarchitectural axioms~\cite{norman2023pipesynth,hsiao2021rtl2uspec} have also been synthesized. Isla~\cite{armstrong2021isla} evaluates litmus tests against full ISA semantics~\cite{armstrong2019sail}, and TransForm~\cite{hossain2020transform} synthesizes litmus tests from axiomatic transistency models. \toolname{} synthesizes security litmus tests from a defense's specification.
